From d7145e39fe2c53f4a9dfd3a7149d2a16bb2d2c06 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 17:32:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Add audio: even out the volume, simpler form, give it to
 a tonie

- Loudness levelling in the browser (ITU-R BS.1770 / EBU R128, -16 LUFS like the server's loudnorm, look-ahead peak limiter at -1.5 dBFS, max +18 dB). It runs on both upload paths (browser encoding and PCM upload), so encode.normalize now applies to every upload, not just server-side conversion of library files. Measured within 0.05 LU of ffmpeg ebur128.
- The form after picking files: file count, Sort A-Z, Name, Save in, Even out the volume, and a More options switch for browser vs server conversion; one full-width Add to library button.
- After adding, pick the tonie that should play it: sets source=lib://..., nocloud=true and live=false in one tap.
- Dev proxy forwards /content so tonie settings can be saved with a relative API URL.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VdeEDs6BS9YupCSmfGg7F8
